@events
id|date|category|stage|status|title|before|after|affected|announced|assent|effective|end|sources|note
income-baseline|1960|income|baseline|context|1960 starting point: progressive income tax|Federal personal income tax already existed.|Progressive income taxation is the starting regime, not a tax introduced in 1960.|Individuals|||1960||HISTORY|No complete 1960 rate schedule is asserted. Early annual rate changes remain a coverage gap.
cgt-baseline|1960|cgt|baseline|context|1960 starting point: no general CGT|Ordinary income and profit-making transactions could be taxable.|No comprehensive capital-gains regime; that does not mean every asset-sale profit was exempt.|Asset owners|||1960||HISTORY|Baseline, not an abolition event. Later pre-CGT exemptions have exceptions.
gearing-baseline|1960|gearing|baseline|context|1960 starting point: income-producing expenses|General income-tax deduction principles already applied.|Negative gearing is an outcome of deductible investment expenses exceeding income, not a separate tax or a new 1960 concession.|Investors|||1960||HISTORY;NG_HISTORY|No discrete introduction date is claimed. This review focuses on rental-property restrictions and reversals.
consumption-baseline|1960|consumption|baseline|context|1960 starting point: wholesale sales tax|Wholesale sales tax had operated since 1930.|A selective goods tax preceded GST; there was no general GST in 1960.|Goods suppliers and consumers|||1960||HISTORY|No complete historical sales-tax item/rate schedule is transcribed.
excise-baseline|1960|excise|baseline|context|1960 starting point: excise already established|Alcohol, tobacco and petroleum were already taxed.|Existing excise systems form the baseline; petrol excise predates 1960 and on-road diesel excise began in 1957.|Fuel, tobacco and alcohol supply chains|||1960||FUEL_HISTORY;TOBACCO;HISTORY|Domestic excise and excise-equivalent customs duty on imports are distinguished where relevant.
trust-baseline|1960|trusts|baseline|context|1960 starting point: beneficiary and trustee taxation|Division 6 of the 1936 income-tax legislation already governed trust income.|Liability could fall on beneficiaries or trustees; a trust was not automatically tax-free.|Trustees and beneficiaries|||1960||TRUST64;BAMFORD|Baseline summary, not a complete reconstruction of the 1960 Act.
trust-99a|1964|trusts|effective|historical_law|Section 99A: retained trust income|Trustee assessments operated under earlier rules.|A special trustee-tax regime for relevant undistributed income was introduced.|Affected trustees|||1964||TRUST64|Year precision only; commencement day and original rate are not independently transcribed. Exceptions matter.
wine-wst|1974|consumption|effective|historical_law|Wholesale sales tax applied to wine|Wine had been subject to varying historical arrangements.|Wholesale sales tax became the continuing wine-tax framework later replaced by WET.|Wine supplies|||1974||WET|Year precision; the rate changed subsequently. The 41% rate belongs to the pre-GST endpoint, not necessarily 1974.
income-1975|1975|income|effective|historical_law|Income-tax scale restructured|Fourteen steps in the personal rate scale.|Seven steps following the 1975 Budget restructuring.|Individuals|||1975||ASPREY|Year precision. A complete set of rates, rebates and transitional averages is not included.
income-indexation|1976-07-01|income|effective|historical_law|Personal income-tax indexation introduced|Nominal scales were adjusted by discretionary decisions.|Indexation of the personal rate scale and some rebates from 1976–77.|Individuals|||1976-07-01||ASPREY|Indexation was later curtailed and ceased; this is not a claim of continuous indexation since 1976.
income-indexation-end|1979-07-01|income|expiry|historical_law|Income-tax indexation ceased|The late-1970s indexation arrangements applied.|Indexation ceased in the 1979–80 income year in the cited historical study.|Individuals|||1979-07-01||ASPREY|Income-year boundary used; not an independently verified repeal-assent date. Intermediate reductions are not fully catalogued.
trust-s100a|1979|trusts|enactment|historical_law|Section 100A reimbursement-agreement rule|Existing trust assessment and anti-avoidance provisions applied.|Reimbursement arrangements could trigger trustee assessment rather than the apparent beneficiary treatment.|Trustees and beneficiaries|||||S100A|Enactment-year precision; retrospective application boundaries are not reconstructed. Ordinary family or commercial dealings are excluded; later ATO guidance is a separate event.
trust-minors|1980|trusts|enactment|historical_law|Special rules for minors' unearned income|Income splitting with minors could benefit from ordinary rates.|Division 6AA introduced special treatment for eligible income of minors, with excepted persons and income.|Minors and trusts distributing income to them|||||MINORS|Enactment-year record, not an exact income-year commencement; employment and qualifying estate-derived income are not automatically subject to penalty rates. Original brackets are not reconstructed.
fuel-rebate|1982|excise|effective|historical_law|Diesel Fuel Rebate Scheme|Off-road diesel had generally been outside the on-road excise base.|Off-road diesel was brought into the system with rebates for eligible uses.|Diesel users|||1982||FUEL_HISTORY|Year precision; a rebate is distinct from a general zero rate for every off-road use.
excise-cpi|1983|excise|effective|historical_law|Excise rates linked to CPI|Changes depended on discretionary rate decisions.|Automatic CPI indexation introduced for major excise categories.|Fuel, tobacco and alcohol|||1983||FUEL_HISTORY;TOBACCO|Year-level policy event. Routine subsequent indexation notices are not all separate timeline records.
medicare-start|1984|income|effective|historical_law|Medicare levy introduced|No Medicare levy under the new Medicare scheme.|A separate levy accompanied Medicare, in addition to ordinary income-tax scales.|Liable individuals|||1984||MARGINAL|This record does not supply an independently audited original levy-rate schedule or confuse Medicare with the earlier Medibank levy.
gearing-quarantine|1985-07|gearing|effective|historical_law|Rental interest losses quarantined|Rental interest could contribute to losses offset against other assessable income.|Interest deductions for affected rental investments were restricted against rental income rather than unrelated income.|Affected rental investors|||1985-07|1987-06-30|NG_HISTORY;NG_DATES|Month precision. Not an abolition of all rental deductions or of negative gearing for every asset class; detailed acquisition exemptions are not reconstructed.
cgt-start|1985-09-20|cgt|effective|historical_law|General capital gains tax introduced|No comprehensive CGT regime.|CGT applied to relevant assets acquired from 20 September 1985, with exemptions and indexation arrangements.|Individuals, trusts and other asset owners|||1985-09-20||HISTORY|CGT forms part of income tax, not a separate flat-rate tax. The main residence generally received an exemption.
trust-public|1985|trusts|effective|historical_law|Public trading trusts taxed on a company-like basis|Public unit trusts could provide an alternative to company structures.|Division 6C introduced company-like treatment for public trading trusts within its scope.|Public trading trusts|||1985||PUBLIC_TRUST|Year precision. Not a blanket company tax on private family trusts or passive investment trusts.
fbt-start|1986|income|effective|historical_law|Fringe benefits tax introduced|Non-cash employee remuneration was less comprehensively taxed.|A separate employer-level tax broadened taxation of remuneration benefits.|Employers providing taxable fringe benefits|||1986||HISTORY|Adjacent remuneration tax, not a personal marginal-rate increase. Exact first FBT-year details are not reconstructed.
imputation-start|1987|income|effective|historical_law|Dividend imputation introduced|Company profits and shareholder dividends could be taxed without imputation credits.|Eligible Australian company tax could be recognised through franking credits for shareholders.|Shareholders receiving franked dividends|||1987||HISTORY|Year precision; refundability of excess credits was a later reform.
gearing-restored|1987-07-01|gearing|effective|historical_law|Rental negative gearing restored|Affected rental interest had been quarantined.|Full interest deductibility against other income was restored; rental building allowances were also reduced.|Rental property investors|||1987-07-01||NG_HISTORY;NG_DATES|Effective income-year boundary. The government announcement came later; the exact announcement date is not entered.
lito-start|1993|income|effective|historical_law|Low income tax offset introduced|Ordinary rates and existing rebates applied.|A low-income offset was introduced, initially with a maximum of $150.|Eligible lower-income taxpayers|||1993||MARGINAL|Year precision; this is LITO, not the later temporary LMITO. Tapers and amounts subsequently changed.
income-1994|1994-07-01|income|baseline|context|1994–95 rate-threshold benchmark|Earlier annual schedules are not fully transcribed.|Thresholds in the Treasury series: $5,400, $20,700, $38,000 and $50,000.|Resident individuals|||1994-07-01||THRESHOLDS|Benchmark, not an assertion that every threshold changed on this date. Rates themselves are not supplied for this benchmark.
trust-loss-cutoff|1995-05-09|trusts|announcement|historical_law|Trust-loss reform application boundary|Trust losses were less constrained by the later integrity tests.|The announced trust-loss measures used a 7:30pm EST 9 May 1995 application boundary.|Trusts seeking to deduct losses|1995-05-09||1995-05-09||TRUST_LOSS|Announcement/application boundary, not enactment in 1995. Later family-trust election and distribution-tax details require the enacted legislation.
excise-franchise|1997-08|excise|effective|historical_law|Federal excise replaces state franchise-fee revenue|State franchise fees operated alongside federal excise.|Federal excise/surcharges increased after the state-fee invalidations.|Fuel and tobacco supplies|||1997-08||FUEL_HISTORY;TOBACCO|Month precision. State legal changes are context for the Commonwealth change, not a state-tax timeline.
div7a-start|1997-12-04|trusts|effective|historical_law|Division 7A application begins|Private-company benefits could escape ordinary dividend treatment.|Relevant payments, loans and debt forgiveness to shareholders or associates can be deemed dividends.|Private companies, associates and trust structures|||1997-12-04||DIV7A|Inserted by a 1998 Act, with this earlier application date. Not every trust entitlement is necessarily a loan; see Bendel 2026.
trust-ftdt|1998|trusts|enactment|historical_law|Family trust election and distribution-tax framework|Trust-loss integrity reforms had been announced with a 1995 boundary.|The 1998 framework couples family/interposed-entity elections with distribution tax for relevant distributions outside the family group.|Trusts and interposed entities making elections|||||FTDT;TRUST_LOSS|Year of legislation, not a claim that all applications start in 1998. Exact rates and retrospective application depend on the relevant law; not a tax on every ordinary trust distribution.
cgt-discount|1999-09-21|cgt|effective|historical_law|CGT discount replaces ongoing indexation for eligible gains|Indexation and averaging arrangements applied.|Eligible individuals and trusts gained a 50% discount for assets held at least 12 months; pre-change holdings retained an indexation choice subject to rules.|Eligible individuals and trusts|||1999-09-21||CGT99|Change applied from 11:45am ACT time. The discount reduces the taxable gain, not the marginal tax rate; companies do not receive the individual 50% discount.
cgt-small|1999-09-21|cgt|effective|historical_law|Small-business CGT concessions consolidated|Earlier concessions operated separately.|Four concessions: 15-year exemption, active-asset reduction, retirement exemption and rollover.|Eligible small-business disposals|||1999-09-21||CGT_SMALL|Separate eligibility tests and limits apply. They are not automatic concessions on every investment asset.
tobacco-stick|1999-11|excise|effective|historical_law|Cigarette excise moves to a per-stick basis|Cigarettes were taxed under a weight-based system.|Per-stick treatment replaced weight-based cigarette excise; other tobacco remained weight-based.|Cigarette and loose-tobacco supplies|||1999-11||TOBACCO|Month precision. Later conversion-factor changes for loose tobacco are distinct.
gst-start|2000-07-01|consumption|effective|historical_law|GST introduced at 10%; wholesale sales tax removed|Selective wholesale sales taxes operated.|A 10% GST applied to taxable supplies with input tax credits; wholesale sales tax was replaced.|Taxable supplies and registered enterprises|||2000-07-01||GST_HISTORY;HISTORY|GST-free and input-taxed supplies differ. Basic food, many health/education supplies and residential rent require their specific rules.
wine-wet|2000-07-01|consumption|effective|historical_law|Wine Equalisation Tax introduced|Wine wholesale sales tax was 41% immediately before reform.|29% WET on the relevant wholesale value, alongside GST.|Wine supplies|||2000-07-01||WET|WET is value-based, not alcohol-volume excise. Producer rebates and special valuation rules are not fully catalogued.
income-2000|2000-07-01|income|effective|historical_law|Income-tax thresholds reset with GST reform|Treasury benchmark thresholds: $5,400 / $20,700 / $38,000 / $50,000.|Thresholds became $6,000 / $20,000 / $50,000 / $60,000.|Resident individuals|||2000-07-01||THRESHOLDS|Threshold changes only in this record; levies, offsets and the full rate scale must also be considered.
franking-refundable|2000-07-01|income|effective|historical_law|Excess franking credits become refundable|Credits generally offset tax payable without a cash refund of excess credits.|Eligible recipients could obtain refunds of excess franking credits.|Eligible shareholders|||2000-07-01||HISTORY|Eligibility and integrity rules apply. A refund of company tax is not a new untaxed dividend.
fuel-gst|2000-07-01|excise|effective|historical_law|Fuel excise reduced alongside GST|Pre-GST fuel excise rates applied.|Petrol and diesel excise reduced by 6.656 cents per litre as GST began.|Petrol and diesel supplies|||2000-07-01||FUEL_HISTORY|Excise reduction and GST introduction are different taxes; not a 6.656c claim about the final pump price.
fuel-index-stop|2001|excise|effective|historical_law|Fuel excise cut and indexation stopped|Petroleum excise was CPI-indexed.|A 1.5c/litre reduction accompanied cessation of petroleum indexation, with limited exceptions.|Petroleum supplies|||2001||FUEL_HISTORY|Year precision. The indexation pause did not apply to all alcohol or tobacco taxes.
income-2003|2003-07-01|income|effective|historical_law|Personal income-tax thresholds increased|Thresholds: $6,000 / $20,000 / $50,000 / $60,000.|Thresholds: $6,000 / $21,600 / $52,000 / $62,500.|Resident individuals|||2003-07-01||THRESHOLDS|Nominal dollars; this is not an inflation-adjusted tax-burden comparison.
income-2004|2004-07-01|income|effective|historical_law|Upper personal income-tax thresholds increased|Upper thresholds: $52,000 and $62,500.|Upper thresholds: $58,000 and $70,000; lower thresholds unchanged.|Resident individuals|||2004-07-01||THRESHOLDS|Threshold changes, not a complete marginal-rate schedule.
income-2005|2005-07-01|income|effective|historical_law|Upper thresholds increased again|Upper thresholds: $58,000 and $70,000.|Upper thresholds: $63,000 and $95,000; lower thresholds $6,000 and $21,600.|Resident individuals|||2005-07-01||THRESHOLDS|Other rate and offset changes are not reconstructed in this threshold-only record.
income-2006|2006-07-01|income|effective|historical_law|Personal income-tax thresholds substantially widened|Thresholds: $6,000 / $21,600 / $63,000 / $95,000.|Thresholds: $6,000 / $25,000 / $75,000 / $150,000.|Resident individuals|||2006-07-01||THRESHOLDS|Use a complete schedule for tax calculations; these are threshold observations.
income-2007|2007-07-01|income|effective|historical_law|Second personal threshold rises to $30,000|Second threshold $25,000.|Second threshold $30,000; other thresholds $6,000, $75,000 and $150,000.|Resident individuals|||2007-07-01||THRESHOLDS|Threshold-only record.
gst-threshold|2007-07-01|consumption|effective|historical_law|GST registration threshold increased|General registration threshold $50,000.|General registration threshold $75,000.|Businesses other than non-profit bodies|||2007-07-01||GST_LIMIT|Turnover, not profit. Special compulsory-registration rules still apply.
excise-rtd|2008-04-27|excise|effective|historical_law|Ready-to-drink alcohol excise increased|Relevant RTDs: $39.36 per litre of alcohol.|Rate aligned to full-strength spirits: $66.67 per litre of alcohol.|Relevant ready-to-drink alcoholic beverages|||2008-04-27||RTD|Operated initially by tariff proposal; later legislation and validation are described in Treasury's report. These are dollars per litre of alcohol, not per litre of beverage.
income-2008|2008-07-01|income|effective|historical_law|Personal income thresholds rise|Thresholds: $6,000 / $30,000 / $75,000 / $150,000.|Thresholds: $6,000 / $34,000 / $80,000 / $180,000.|Resident individuals|||2008-07-01||THRESHOLDS|Threshold-only record; upper threshold $180,000 persisted for many years.
income-2009|2009-07-01|income|effective|historical_law|2009–10 personal tax scale|Second threshold $34,000; preceding upper-middle rate 40%.|Second threshold $35,000; 2009–10 schedule shown below, including a 38% upper-middle rate.|Resident individuals|||2009-07-01||THRESHOLDS;MARGINAL|Schedule excludes Medicare, LITO and other offsets. Changes are not an inflation-adjusted comparison.
trust-bamford|2010-03-30|trusts|judgment|interpretation|Bamford: trust income and proportionate assessment|Meaning of trust income and the beneficiary's share were contested.|The High Court clarified the trust-law income basis and proportionate approach to beneficiary assessment.|Trustees and beneficiaries|||2010-03-30||BAMFORD|Judicial interpretation, not a newly enacted tax. Deed terms and valid trustee decisions remain important.
tobacco-25|2010-04-29|excise|effective|historical_law|Tobacco excise increased by 25%|Existing indexed excise rates.|One-off 25% additional rate increase.|Tobacco products|||2010-04-29||TOBACCO|Treasury dates the change to 29 April; not a claim that retail prices rose by exactly 25%.
income-2010|2010-07-01|income|effective|historical_law|2010–11 personal income-tax changes|$35,000 second threshold and 38% upper-middle rate.|$37,000 second threshold and 37% upper-middle rate.|Resident individuals|||2010-07-01||THRESHOLDS;RATES|Complete selected rate schedule below excludes offsets and levies.
trust-stream|2010-07-01|trusts|effective|historical_law|Trust capital-gain and franked-distribution streaming|The prior trust assessment framework created uncertainty about tax streaming.|Specific rules enabled streaming of gains and franked distributions, subject to entitlement and integrity requirements.|Trusts and beneficiaries|||2010-07-01||STREAM|2010–11 application boundary for amendments enacted in 2011. Not proof that every trust can stream every income category.
flood-start|2011-07-01|income|effective|historical_law|Temporary flood levy|Ordinary income tax and other applicable levies.|One-year levy for non-exempt individuals above $50,000 taxable income.|Liable individuals|||2011-07-01|2012-06-30|FLOOD|Exemptions applied, including for affected people. This is separate from Medicare.
flood-end|2012-07-01|income|expiry|historical_law|Flood levy expires|Flood levy applied for 2011–12.|No flood levy for the 2012–13 income year under that one-year measure.|Individuals|||2012-07-01||FLOOD|Expiry of a temporary measure, not a new threshold cut.
cgt-nonresident|2012-05-08|cgt|effective|historical_law|Foreign-resident CGT discount restricted|Eligible foreign residents could access the general individual discount.|Discount availability restricted for foreign/temporary resident periods after 8 May 2012, with transitional calculations.|Foreign and temporary residents|||2012-05-08||CGT_FOREIGN|Announcement boundary; resident periods and pre-change gains need apportionment. Not blanket CGT exemption or blanket loss of every discount.
income-2012|2012-07-01|income|effective|historical_law|Tax-free threshold rises to $18,200|Statutory tax-free threshold $6,000.|Threshold $18,200; first positive rate 19%, next rate 32.5%; offsets also changed.|Resident individuals|||2012-07-01||THRESHOLDS;RATES|A tripling of the statutory threshold is not a tripling of everyone's effective tax-free income.
tobacco-annual|2013|excise|effective|historical_law|Program of additional tobacco increases begins|Indexation and earlier discretionary uplifts.|A series of 12.5% annual increases began, ultimately extending through 2020.|Tobacco products|||2013|2020|TOBACCO|Year precision; grouped program, not eight separately counted policy reforms. Subsequent legislated extension is included in the program description.
tobacco-awote|2014-03-01|excise|effective|historical_law|Tobacco indexation changes from CPI to wages|CPI-based indexation.|Indexation linked to Average Weekly Ordinary Time Earnings (AWOTE).|Tobacco products|||2014-03-01||TOBACCO|Distinct from the additional 12.5% increases; routine indexing amounts are not separately transcribed.
medicare-2|2014-07-01|income|effective|historical_law|Medicare levy increases to 2%|Standard Medicare levy 1.5%.|Standard rate 2%, subject to low-income reductions and exemptions.|Liable individuals|||2014-07-01||MEDICARE14;RATES|The Medicare levy surcharge is a different charge. Earlier levy-rate steps are a stated coverage gap.
repair-start|2014-07-01|income|effective|historical_law|Temporary Budget Repair Levy begins|Ordinary personal rates plus applicable levies.|Additional 2% on taxable income above $180,000 for three income years.|Higher-income individuals|||2014-07-01|2017-06-30|LEVY14|Do not present the temporary levy as a permanent increase in the ordinary top bracket.
fuel-index-return|2014-11-10|excise|effective|historical_law|Fuel excise indexation restored|Long pause in petroleum excise indexation.|CPI indexation resumed.|Relevant fuel products|||2014-11-10||FUEL_HISTORY|Policy commencement, not a list of every subsequent February/August rate notice.
trust-amit|2016-07-01|trusts|effective|historical_law|Attribution regime for eligible managed investment trusts|Eligible MITs used the earlier trust-tax framework.|Elective attribution managed investment trust regime applied from 2016–17, with early adoption available.|Eligible managed investment trusts|||2016-07-01||AMIT|Not a new tax on all family trusts. The elective regime has eligibility and attribution rules.
income-2016|2016-07-01|income|effective|historical_law|37% bracket threshold rises to $87,000|37% marginal rate began above $80,000.|37% marginal rate began above $87,000.|Resident individuals|||2016-07-01||RATES|Full selected schedule below; temporary Budget Repair Levy still applied separately during 2016–17.
repair-end|2017-07-01|income|expiry|historical_law|Temporary Budget Repair Levy ends|Additional 2% above $180,000.|The three-year additional levy ceased.|Individuals|||2017-07-01||LEVY14|Ordinary top marginal rate and Medicare levy remained separate.
rental-travel|2017-07-01|gearing|effective|historical_law|Residential rental travel deductions restricted|Qualifying rental-related travel could be deductible.|Travel deductions generally denied for affected residential rental investors.|Affected rental investors|||2017-07-01||RENT_TRAVEL|Business/entity exceptions apply. Disallowed travel is not automatically added to the CGT cost base.
rental-depreciation|2017-07-01|gearing|effective|historical_law|Second-hand rental plant depreciation restricted|Investors could generally claim decline in value of eligible acquired plant.|Deductions limited for second-hand depreciating assets in affected residential rental properties.|Affected residential rental investors|2017-05-09||2017-07-01||RENT_ASSETS|Acquisition-time grandfathering and business/entity exceptions apply. Capital-works deductions are different.
gst-digital|2017-07-01|consumption|effective|historical_law|GST extends to imported digital products and services|Many offshore consumer supplies fell outside collection rules.|GST applied to relevant offshore services/digital supplies to Australian consumers.|Offshore suppliers and Australian consumers|||2017-07-01||GST_IMPORT|Registration and business-to-business rules apply. Rate remains 10%; this is a base/collection change.
gst-lowvalue|2018-07-01|consumption|effective|historical_law|GST extends to low-value imported goods|Many goods at or below the low-value customs threshold escaped GST collection.|Offshore suppliers/platforms must collect GST on eligible low-value consumer imports.|Relevant imported goods and suppliers|||2018-07-01||GST_IMPORT|Generally goods of A$1,000 or less, subject to the scheme's rules. Not a new customs tariff on every parcel.
income-2018|2018-07-01|income|effective|historical_law|37% bracket threshold rises to $90,000|37% marginal rate began above $87,000.|37% marginal rate began above $90,000.|Resident individuals|||2018-07-01||RATES|Part of the staged personal income-tax plan; later stages were subsequently changed.
lmito-start|2018-07-01|income|effective|historical_law|Low and middle income tax offset introduced|LITO existed, but not LMITO.|A separate temporary offset applied from 2018–19; subsequent legislation increased its amount.|Eligible resident individuals|||2018-07-01|2022-06-30|OFFSETS|The initial maximum and every extension are not separately reconstructed. Do not backdate the final $1,500 amount to 2018.
vacant-deductions|2019-07-01|gearing|effective|historical_law|Holding-cost deductions restricted for vacant land|General deduction principles could allow qualifying holding costs.|Specified vacant-land holding costs became non-deductible unless an exclusion applied.|Affected landowners|||2019-07-01||VACANT|This is broader than residential rental negative gearing; business and entity exclusions matter.
tobacco-import|2019-07-01|excise|effective|historical_law|Tobacco taxing point brought forward|Duty could be deferred while tobacco was in licensed warehouses.|Taxing point moved to importation/manufacture under the integrity reforms.|Tobacco supply chain|||2019-07-01||TOBACCO|Collection timing change, not a new percentage rate.
cgt-home-law|2019|cgt|enactment|historical_law|Foreign-resident main-residence exemption removed|Foreign residents could qualify under the earlier exemption.|Legislation removed access for affected disposals, with a transitional window and limited life-event exceptions.|People foreign-resident for tax purposes at disposal|2017-05-09||2017-05-09||CGT_HOME;CGT2020|Enactment year only. Rules reach back to the 9 May 2017 announcement; eligible older holdings had relief through 30 June 2020.
cgt-home-transition|2020-07-01|cgt|expiry|historical_law|Foreign-resident main-home transition ends|Qualifying pre-announcement properties could be disposed of by 30 June 2020 under transitional relief.|The transition no longer protected later disposals.|Affected foreign-resident vendors|||2020-07-01||CGT_HOME|Life-event exceptions and residency at disposal remain relevant. Citizenship is not the test.
income-2020|2020-07-01|income|effective|historical_law|Stage 2 personal tax cuts brought forward|19% bracket ended at $37,000; 37% bracket began at $90,000.|Thresholds changed to $45,000 and $120,000 for 2020–21.|Resident individuals|||2020-07-01||RATES|Application to the full income year differs from the later parliamentary and payroll-withholding implementation dates.
lmito-2022|2021-07-01|income|effective|historical_law|LMITO increased for its final income year|Maximum offset $1,080.|Maximum $1,500 following the additional $420 for 2021–22.|Eligible taxpayers|2022-03-29||2021-07-01|2022-06-30|LMITO22;OFFSETS|Retrospective income-year application; not a policy announcement made in July 2021. Offsets are non-refundable.
fuel-2022-cut|2022-03-30|excise|effective|historical_law|Fuel excise temporarily halved|Ordinary indexed rates.|50% reduction for six months.|Relevant fuel supplies|||2022-03-30|2022-09-28|FUEL_HISTORY|The 2022 relief episode is separate from the 2026 episode.
lmito-end|2022-07-01|income|expiry|historical_law|LMITO ceases to apply|LMITO available through 2021–22.|No LMITO for 2022–23 and later years under that measure.|Previously eligible taxpayers|||2022-07-01||OFFSETS|LITO continued; a tax return lodged later for 2021–22 could still claim that year's entitlement.
fuel-2022-end|2022-09-29|excise|expiry|historical_law|Six-month fuel-excise relief ends|Temporary 50% reduction.|Full excise arrangements resumed.|Relevant fuel supplies|||2022-09-29||FUEL_HISTORY|No assumption of immediate or exact pass-through to pump prices.
trust-s100a-guidance|2022-12-08|trusts|guidance|interpretation|ATO finalises section 100A ruling|The statutory anti-avoidance rule already existed.|TR 2022/4 set out the Commissioner's interpretation of reimbursement agreements and exclusions.|Trustees, beneficiaries and advisers|||2022-12-08||S100A|Guidance, not a new trust-tax statute. Court decisions and facts may affect its application.
tobacco-2023|2023-09-01|excise|effective|historical_law|Additional 5% tobacco uplift and loose-leaf adjustment|Ordinary wage indexation and existing conversion factor.|First of three additional annual 5% uplifts; loose-leaf conversion transition toward 0.6g per stick-equivalent began.|Tobacco products|||2023-09-01||TOBACCO25|Additional uplift, not the entire annual percentage change. Implemented through tariff arrangements and later legislation.
income-2024-passed|2024-02-27|income|enactment|historical_law|Revised Stage 3 design passes Parliament|Previously legislated future Stage 3 design.|Parliament passed the replacement personal income-tax cuts for July 2024.|Resident individuals|2024-01-25||2024-07-01||PASS24;CUT24|Parliamentary passage is not Royal Assent. This event records passage; the exact assent date is not independently entered.
income-2024|2024-07-01|income|effective|historical_law|Revised Stage 3 tax rates commence|19%, 32.5%, 37%, 45% positive marginal rates under the preceding scale.|16%, 30%, 37%, 45%; upper thresholds $135,000 and $190,000.|Resident individuals|2024-01-25||2024-07-01||CUT24;RATES|Tax-free threshold remains $18,200 and first positive bracket ends at $45,000; Medicare is additional.
tobacco-2024|2024-09-01|excise|effective|historical_law|Second additional 5% tobacco uplift|First uplift already embedded in rates.|A further 5% uplift, additional to normal indexation.|Tobacco products|||2024-09-01||TOBACCO25|One step in a legislated program, not a five-percentage-point ad-valorem sales tax.
cgt-withholding2025|2025-01-01|cgt|effective|enacted|Property CGT withholding rises; value threshold removed|12.5% withholding for relevant property at or above $750,000.|15% withholding; property-value threshold removed.|Australian real-property transactions|||2025-01-01||FRCGW|Withholding is a collection mechanism, not the final CGT rate. Resident vendors normally need clearance certificates; variations may apply.
beer-freeze|2025-08-04|excise|effective|enacted|Draught-beer excise indexation frozen|Relevant draught beer rates normally indexed each February and August.|Four scheduled indexation rounds paused, through February 2027.|Specified draught-beer categories|||2025-08-04||BEER|First skipped scheduled adjustment shown; the legislative freeze window and tariff item scope must be consulted. Packaged beer and spirits are not included.
tobacco-2025|2025-09-01|excise|effective|enacted|Third additional 5% tobacco uplift|Two additional uplifts already applied.|Third 5% uplift, alongside normal indexation and the loose-leaf conversion step.|Tobacco products|||2025-09-01||TOBACCO25|Conversion factor for this step 0.625g; later transition reaches 0.6g. Not every routine excise-rate notice is included.
fuel-2026-announcement|2026-03-30|excise|announcement|enacted|2026 temporary fuel-excise relief announced|Standard petrol/diesel excise arrangements.|Initial announcement: halve excise from 1 April to 30 June, a 26.3c/litre reduction.|Petrol and diesel supplies|2026-03-30||2026-04-01|2026-06-30|FUEL26_A|This records the initial announcement, not a complete ledger of later April adjustments. No claim of an exact realised pump-price reduction.
fuel-2026-start|2026-04-01|excise|effective|enacted|2026 temporary fuel relief begins|Ordinary fuel excise rates.|Temporary fuel-excise reductions apply during April–June.|Petrol and diesel supplies|2026-03-30||2026-04-01|2026-06-30|FUEL26_A;FUEL26_END|Later additional relief within this window is not numerically reconstructed; use official rate notices for transactions.
reform2026-budget|2026-05-12|cgt|announcement|enacted|Budget announces CGT and rental-loss reform|50% discount and existing rental-loss rules applied.|Reforms announced with distinct asset-acquisition and gain-accrual boundaries.|Affected investors|2026-05-12||2027-07-01||FACT26;ACT26|7:30pm AEST acquisition cutoff matters for rental losses; CGT reform applies prospectively to gains accruing from July 2027. Not an immediate blanket tax-rate change.
trust-bendel|2026-06-10|trusts|judgment|interpretation|Bendel: High Court decides unpaid-entitlement question|ATO and taxpayers disputed whether an unpaid trust entitlement constituted a Division 7A loan.|The appeal was dismissed: on these trust terms, amounts set aside on separate trust were not the alleged Division 7A loans.|Corporate beneficiaries and associated trusts|||2026-06-10||BENDEL|Court interpretation, not repeal of Division 7A. Separate loans, other benefit rules and later ATO responses still require review.
reform2026-act|2026-06-26|cgt|enactment|enacted|First tranche of 2026 tax reform receives assent|Budget measures were proposals.|Act No.49 enacts the core CGT, negative-gearing, worker-offset and standard-deduction framework.|Affected investors and workers|2026-05-12|2026-06-26|2026-06-26||ACT26;REFORM26|Assent does not make every measure operative on this date: substantive application dates differ. Later technical reforms remain separate.
income-2026|2026-07-01|income|effective|enacted|First personal rate falls from 16% to 15%|16% on income above $18,200 up to $45,000.|15% on that band; other ordinary marginal rates unchanged.|Resident individuals|||2026-07-01||CUT26;CURRENT|Up to $268 less basic income tax than the 16% schedule, calculated as 1% × $26,800. Excludes offsets and levies.
worker-deduction|2026-07-01|income|effective|enacted|Standard work-related deduction begins|Taxpayers generally claimed eligible itemised work expenses.|Eligible workers can use a standard deduction up to $1,000, or claim eligible actual expenses instead.|Eligible workers|2026-05-12|2026-06-26|2026-07-01||ACT26;REFORM26|A deduction reduces taxable income, not tax dollar-for-dollar. Eligibility, labour-income limit, separately deductible categories and no-double-counting rules apply.
fuel-2026-july|2026-07-01|excise|effective|enacted|Fuel relief tapers to a 16c/litre reduction|April–June temporary relief.|A 16c/litre excise reduction applies from 1 July through 2 August.|Petrol and diesel supplies|2026-06-22||2026-07-01|2026-08-02|FUEL26_B|Recorded reduction relative to normal settings, not the absolute excise rate.
fuel-2026-end|2026-08-03|excise|expiry|enacted|Temporary 2026 fuel-tax relief ends|16c/litre reduction applied through 2 August.|Temporary relief ended and ordinary indexed arrangements resumed.|Fuel suppliers and users|||2026-08-03||FUEL26_END|Routine indexation on the same date is distinct from withdrawal of temporary relief.
trust2026-bill|2026-10-14|trusts|proposal|proposed|30% discretionary-trust minimum tax Bill introduced|Existing trust-tax rules, without the proposed general 30% minimum.|Bill proposes trustee-level minimum tax from July 2028, beneficiary offsets, exclusions and restructuring/election options.|Discretionary trusts within the proposed scope|2026-05-12||2028-07-01||TRUST26|Introduced No.3 Bill, not verified as assented law at this review date. Fixed, charitable, qualifying testamentary and other specified arrangements are treated differently.
reform2026-details|2026-10-14|gearing|proposal|proposed|Further CGT and negative-gearing details introduced|Core framework enacted in June; technical details consulted on separately.|No.3 Bill adds CGT trust interactions and new-dwelling/exemption provisions.|Affected investors and trusts|||2027-07-01||TRUST26;DRAFT26|Do not merge these pending details into the June Act as if already enacted. Enactment not verified as at 15 October.
income-2027|2027-07-01|income|scheduled|enacted_future|Next personal rate cut: 15% to 14%|15% on the first positive resident band.|Legislated further reduction to 14% on income above $18,200 up to $45,000.|Resident individuals|||2027-07-01||CUT26|Future commencement known at the review date. No assumption about laws enacted after 15 October 2026.
cgt-2027|2027-07-01|cgt|scheduled|enacted_future|CGT indexation and 30% minimum framework|Eligible long-held gains generally received a 50% discount.|Core reform replaces the discount for affected post-June-2027 gains with inflation-adjusted cost bases and a 30% minimum-tax framework.|Affected individuals and trusts|2026-05-12|2026-06-26|2027-07-01||ACT26;FACT26;REFORM26|Not 30% of the sale price. Transition, pre-1985 assets, holding periods, new housing, qualifying affordable housing, small-business concessions and minimum-tax exemptions require the specific rules.
gearing-2027|2027-07-01|gearing|scheduled|enacted_future|Rental-loss quarantine for affected existing dwellings|Qualifying rental losses could offset unrelated income.|Losses on affected existing dwellings purchased after 7:30pm AEST 12 May 2026 limited to residential-property income, with carry-forward.|Affected residential investors|2026-05-12|2026-06-26|2027-07-01||ACT26;FACT26;REFORM26|Earlier holdings generally grandfathered; new builds and specified housing arrangements excepted. Shares and commercial property are not covered by this residential rule; later Bill details remain pending.
wato-2027|2027-07-01|income|scheduled|enacted_future|Working Australians Tax Offset begins|Existing rate scale and applicable offsets.|New non-refundable worker offset of up to $250 annually.|Eligible workers|2026-05-12|2026-06-26|2027-07-01||ACT26;WORK26|An offset reduces tax payable; this is separate from the $1,000 deduction and the 14% rate cut.
trust-2028|2028-07-01|trusts|scheduled|proposed|Proposed trust minimum-tax commencement|Existing enacted trust framework remains the legal baseline at review.|Proposed 30% trustee-level minimum, with non-refundable beneficiary offsets for relevant non-corporate beneficiaries.|Discretionary trusts within proposed scope|2026-05-12||2028-07-01||TRUST26|Conditional future date only. No Royal Assent verified; do not use this row as current law or assume every family or testamentary trust is included.
